### Detailed Technical Study: Java Enumerations (enum) Architecture & Switch Integration

#### 1. Why Enums are Full Classes in Java:
Unlike in C/C++ where enums are simply named integer constants, an `enum` in Java is a full-fledged class.
- The JVM creates exactly one instance of each enum constant, making them immutable singletons.
- They can define constructors, fields, and custom instance methods.
- Every enum automatically inherits `name()`, `ordinal()`, and `values()` from `java.lang.Enum`.

#### 2. Enum Methods Inherited from `java.lang.Enum`:
| Method | Return Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`values()`** | `EnumClass[]` | Returns an array containing all constants in their declared order. |
| **`ordinal()`** | `int` | Returns the numeric index position of the constant (0-indexed). |
| **`name()`** | `String` | Returns the exact identifier name as declared. |
| **`valueOf(String s)`** | `EnumClass` | Parses a string into its matching enum constant. |

#### 3. Complete Demonstrative Java Implementation:
```java
enum CourseGrade {
    GRADE_O(10, "Outstanding"),
    GRADE_A_PLUS(9, "Excellent"),
    GRADE_A(8, "Very Good"),
    GRADE_B_PLUS(7, "Good"),
    GRADE_F(0, "Fail");

    private final int gradePoint;
    private final String description;

    // Enum constructors are strictly private
    CourseGrade(int gradePoint, String description) {
        this.gradePoint = gradePoint;
        this.description = description;
    }

    public int getGradePoint() { return gradePoint; }
    public String getDescription() { return description; }
}

public class EnumDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        CourseGrade myGrade = CourseGrade.GRADE_A_PLUS;

        // Displaying enum metadata
        System.out.println("Grade Name:     " + myGrade.name());
        System.out.println("Grade Ordinal:  " + myGrade.ordinal());
        System.out.println("Grade Point:    " + myGrade.getGradePoint());
        System.out.println("Description:    " + myGrade.getDescription());

        // Switch Statement Integration
        System.out.print("Evaluation:     ");
        switch (myGrade) {
            case GRADE_O:
            case GRADE_A_PLUS:
                System.out.println("Eligible for Academic Honors!");
                break;
            case GRADE_A:
            case GRADE_B_PLUS:
                System.out.println("Cleared with High Performance.");
                break;
            case GRADE_F:
                System.out.println("Must re-appear for supplementary examination.");
                break;
        }

        // Iterating over all enum constants
        System.out.println("\nAll Grading Scales in MR-25 Blueprint:");
        for (CourseGrade g : CourseGrade.values()) {
            System.out.printf("  [%d] %-12s: %d Points (%s)\n", g.ordinal(), g.name(), g.getGradePoint(), g.getDescription());
        }
    }
}
```

$$\therefore \text{Java enums provide type-safe constants with rich object-oriented behavior.}$$
